            {
              "id": "a1c8b431-a90a-3a48-88f0-e85170f0ed27",
              "name": "Banned C function detected (strncpy)",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the code uses a string copy operation where the source pointer may be null, and there are no explicit checks to ensure the source is valid before copying. The risk is further highlighted by the classification indicating undefined behavior due to possible null pointers. The destination is a non-null address-of expression, so the main concern is the lack of validation for the source. The use of a constant for the copy size does not mitigate the risk of dereferencing a null pointer. The probability of this being a false positive is low because the analysis detected a real risk of undefined behavior if the source is null.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nBefore performing the string copy operation, ensure that the source pointer is not null. This prevents undefined behavior due to dereferencing a null pointer. For example:\n\n```cpp\nconst char* src_ptr = final_message.str().c_str();\nif (src_ptr != nullptr) {\n    strncpy(reinterpret_cast<char *>(&data_item->message), src_ptr, MAX_EVENT_NOTIFICATION_MSG_SIZE-1);\n    reinterpret_cast<char *>(&data_item->message)[MAX_EVENT_NOTIFICATION_MSG_SIZE-1] = '\\0';\n} else {\n    reinterpret_cast<char *>(&data_item->message)[0] = '\\0'; // or handle error as appropriate\n}\n```\n\nThis approach ensures that the destination buffer is only written to if the source is valid, and it also explicitly null-terminates the destination buffer to avoid unterminated strings.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
