            {
              "id": "7a9aa502-043d-3ffd-8b52-7cb0723ff17a",
              "name": "Banned C function detected (strncpy)",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the code uses a string copy operation where the source pointer may be null, and there are no explicit checks to ensure the source is valid before copying. The classification indicates a risk of undefined behavior if the source pointer is null. The destination is an address-of expression, which is always non-null, so the risk is isolated to the source. The use of a constant for the copy length does not mitigate the risk of a null pointer dereference. The probability of this being a false positive is low because the analysis detected a real possibility of a null source pointer and no guards are present.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nBefore performing the string copy operation, ensure that the source pointer is not null. Add an explicit check for the source pointer and handle the error appropriately, such as by returning early or assigning a default value.\n\n```cpp\nconst char* src_ptr = final_message.str().c_str();\nif (src_ptr != nullptr) {\n    strncpy(reinterpret_cast<char *>(&data_item->message), src_ptr, MAX_EVENT_NOTIFICATION_MSG_SIZE-1);\n    // Optionally, ensure null-termination\n    reinterpret_cast<char *>(&data_item->message)[MAX_EVENT_NOTIFICATION_MSG_SIZE-1] = '\\0';\n} else {\n    // Handle the null case, e.g., set message to an empty string\n    reinterpret_cast<char *>(&data_item->message)[0] = '\\0';\n}\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n\n___\n"
