              "name": "Banned C function detected (strncpy)",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to the possibility that the source pointer (the result of final_message.str().c_str()) may be null, and there are no explicit checks to ensure it is not null before calling the buffer copy function. The destination is an address-of expression and is guaranteed to be non-null, but the source is derived from a string operation that could potentially return a null pointer if the string is empty or uninitialized. The function call does not include any guard or validation for the source pointer, which increases the risk of a crash or undefined behavior. The use of a constant macro for the copy size does not mitigate the null pointer risk. The classification and verdict both indicate a high-confidence, actionable issue.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nBefore performing the buffer copy, ensure that the source string is not null. Add an explicit check to verify that the result of `final_message.str().c_str()` is not a null pointer before calling the copy function. If the source is null, handle the error appropriately (e.g., by setting the destination to an empty string or logging an error).\n\n```cpp\nconst char* src_ptr = final_message.str().c_str();\nif (src_ptr != nullptr) {\n    strncpy(reinterpret_cast<char *>(&data_item->message), src_ptr, MAX_EVENT_NOTIFICATION_MSG_SIZE-1);\n    reinterpret_cast<char *>(&data_item->message)[MAX_EVENT_NOTIFICATION_MSG_SIZE-1] = '\\0'; // Ensure null-termination\n} else {\n    // Handle error: set message to empty string or log error\n    reinterpret_cast<char *>(&data_item->message)[0] = '\\0';\n}\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n\n___\n"
