              "id": "c961bb23-193f-31f4-b8b6-c0cbe0103838",
              "name": "Problematic C function detected (memcpy)",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the destination pointer used in the memory copy operation may be null, and there are no explicit checks to ensure it is valid before the operation. The source is safe, as it is the address of a local variable and cannot be null. However, the destination pointer could be null, which would result in undefined behavior if the memory copy is attempted. The risk is further confirmed by the absence of any guard or validation for the destination pointer. This type of issue can lead to program crashes or more severe security vulnerabilities if exploited.\n\n## In Context Remediation 1\nBefore performing the memory copy, ensure that the destination pointer is not null. Add an explicit check to prevent undefined behavior:\n\n```cpp\nif (metrics_table != nullptr) {\n    std::memcpy(metrics_table, &metrics_tbl, sizeof(amdsmi_hsmp_metrics_table_t));\n} else {\n    // Handle error: destination pointer is null\n    // For example, log an error or return an error code\n}\n```\nThis check prevents the program from attempting to copy memory to a null pointer, which would otherwise result in a crash or undefined behavior.\n\n## In Context Remediation 2\nIf the destination pointer should never be null by design, consider adding an assertion to catch programming errors during development:\n\n```cpp\nassert(metrics_table != nullptr);\nstd::memcpy(metrics_table, &metrics_tbl, sizeof(amdsmi_hsmp_metrics_table_t));\n```\nThis will terminate the program with a clear error message if the pointer is unexpectedly null, making debugging easier.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html)\n\n___\n"
              },
