            {
              "id": "575ef44a-f2da-33c7-b357-78915bf2cf8b",
              "name": "Banned C function detected (strncpy)",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because it is marked as 'UB Risk: possible src/dst overlap (undefined behavior)' and the verdict is 'GENUINE'. The code copies data using a function that is not safe when the source and destination memory regions overlap, which can result in undefined behavior. Dataflow analysis indicates that the source and destination may overlap, increasing the risk. Additionally, the destination pointer may be null, which could also lead to undefined behavior if not properly checked. Although the code ensures a null terminator is written after the copy, this does not mitigate the risk of overlapping memory regions. No explicit guard is present to ensure the destination is valid or that the regions do not overlap.\n\n## In Context Remediation 1\nBefore copying, ensure that the source and destination memory regions do not overlap. Add a runtime check to verify that the memory areas are distinct. If overlap is possible, avoid using functions like `strncpy` that are not safe for overlapping regions.\n\n```cpp\nif (info->build_date != reinterpret_cast<char *>(vbios.date)) {\n    strncpy(info->build_date, reinterpret_cast<char *>(vbios.date), AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH - 1);\n    info->build_date[AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH - 1] = '\\0';\n} else {\n    // Handle the overlap case appropriately, e.g., skip copy or log an error\n}\n```\n\n\n## In Context Remediation 2\nIf overlapping memory regions are possible and must be handled, use a function that is safe for overlapping regions, such as `memmove`. Replace the copy operation with `memmove` and ensure the destination is null-terminated if needed.\n\n```cpp\nmemmove(info->build_date, reinterpret_cast<char *>(vbios.date), AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH - 1);\ninfo->build_date[AMDSMI_MAX_STRING_LENGTH - 1] = '\\0';\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n\n\n___\n"
              },
